      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Nuclear deterrence is the ultimate guarantor of global stability, a grim but necessary evil that prevents the catastrophic wars of the past. The sheer terror of mutual assured destruction forces even the most aggressive powers to the negotiating table, making large-scale conflict unthinkable. Without this ultimate deterrent, the world would descend into a chaotic, brutal conflict where nuclear weapons would be used without restraint.\n\nFor the opposition, the argument that nuclear weapons are inherently immoral is naive and dangerously idealistic. They claim they promote peace, but they ignore the reality that the threat of annihilation is the only thing stopping superpowers from engaging in devastating conventional wars. Their moral stance ignores the practical, brutal calculus of international power politics.",
